+    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
+    # staged point-to-point
+    #
+    # Pipeline parallelism hands one stage's activations to the next rank with
+    # ``isend``/``irecv`` on CUDA tensors. barlink has no direct p2p kernel for
+    # an arbitrary tensor, so the payload is staged exactly like a collective:
+    # D2H into pinned memory on the sender, gloo on the CPU plane, H2D on the
+    # receiver. That is a byte copy, not a conversion, and it is the same two
+    # planes the staged collectives already use.
+    #
+    # The staged send waits for the gloo work before returning. The host
+    # buffer is a local, and a fire-and-forget send would let it be freed while
+    # the transport still owns it; point-to-point callers already have to post
+    # the matching receive independently (a pipeline loop does so before the
+    # forward pass), so the wait cannot deadlock against the peer.
+    # ------------------------------------------------------------------
